// │                                                         │
// └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

IDENTIFY USB
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  lsblk -o NAME,SIZE,MODEL,TRAN,MOUNTPOINTS
                            Show drives + USB devices

  ⚠️ Identify USB by SIZE / MODEL before continuing
  ⚠️ Use /dev/sdX, NOT /dev/sdX1


UNMOUNT USB
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  sudo umount /dev/sdX*
                            Unmount USB partitions


WRITE ISO
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  sudo dd if=~/Downloads/bazzite.iso of=/dev/sdX \
    bs=4M status=progress conv=fsync

                            Write Bazzite ISO to USB

  ⚠️ THIS WILL ERASE THE ENTIRE USB DRIVE


FLUSH / SYNC
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  sync                      Flush pending writes


EJECT
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  sudo eject /dev/sdX      Safely eject USB


QUICK VERSION
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  lsblk -o NAME,SIZE,MODEL,TRAN,MOUNTPOINTS
  sudo umount /dev/sdX*
  sudo dd if=~/Downloads/bazzite.iso of=/dev/sdX bs=4M status=progress conv=fsync
  sync
  sudo eject /dev/sdX


⚠️ Replace /dev/sdX with the ACTUAL USB device.
   Example: /dev/sda — NOT /dev/sda1

Press Enter to return to the menu...
